diff --git a/docs/llvm15-port.md b/docs/llvm15-port.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2006ade
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/llvm15-port.md
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# LLVM 15 port
+
+The P2 backend can be applied to upstream LLVM 15.0.7 (commit
+`8dfdcc7b7bf66834a761bd8de445840ef68e4d1a`). LLVM 15 is the oldest LLVM release
+supported by TinyGo 0.44.0. Using this supported baseline limits unrelated
+compiler changes while preserving the current P2 ABI and hardware helper code.
+
+Create an LLVM 15 checkout or worktree at `llvm15`, then apply the matching
+`llvm15-p2.patch` generated from this port. Do not apply the patch to the legacy
+`llvm-project` checkout: the patch base is the upstream LLVM 15 commit above.
+
+Build in a separate directory. On a modern Linux host with Clang, CMake, Ninja,
+and LLD available, use:
+
+```sh
+cmake -G Ninja -S llvm15/llvm -B ../llvm15-build \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++ \
+  -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS_RELEASE=-O1 -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE=-O1 \
+  -DLLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS='clang;lld' \
+  -DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=X86 -DLLVM_EXPERIMENTAL_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=P2 \
+  -DLLVM_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=ON \
+  -DLLVM_BUILD_LLVM_DYLIB=ON -DLLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB=ON \
+  -DLLVM_USE_LINKER=lld -DLLVM_PARALLEL_LINK_JOBS=1 \
+  -DLLVM_ENABLE_TERMINFO=OFF -DLLVM_ENABLE_LIBXML2=OFF \
+  -DLLVM_ENABLE_ZSTD=OFF -DLLVM_ENABLE_BINDINGS=OFF \
+  -DCLANG_ENABLE_ARCMT=OFF -DCLANG_ENABLE_STATIC_ANALYZER=OFF \
+  -DCLANG_LINK_CLANG_DYLIB=OFF
+ninja -C ../llvm15-build -j4 LLVM libclang clang lld llc llvm-config \
+  llvm-ar llvm-ranlib llvm-nm llvm-objdump llvm-objcopy llvm-readelf \
+  llvm-as llvm-dis llvm-mc llvm-symbolizer llvm-addr2line opt FileCheck not count split-file
+```
+
+The host `-O1` option limits bootstrap time and memory. It does not change the
+optimization level requested when compiling P2 programs. X86 is included for
+TinyGo's host target initialization and host tests. P2 is an experimental LLVM
+target because it is not included in upstream LLVM.
+
+## Target contracts
+
+- Native objects use individual function and data sections, so `--gc-sections`
+  can remove unused runtime exports without LTO. Explicit LUT/cog sections remain
+  as declared. Clang searches its resource headers and the P2 SDK, not host libc.
+- P2 is a 32-bit little-endian target. Hub pointers are byte addresses; cog and
+  LUT instruction locations retain their P2-specific addressing rules.
+- Clang and LLVM agree that 64-bit integers have four-byte natural alignment;
+  double retains eight-byte alignment. C aggregate arguments use inline stack
+  copies marked `byval`, including at calls made from Go. C aggregate results
+  use explicit `sret` pointers before optimization, so C and Go declarations agree.
+- R31 returns a scalar word; R30:R31 returns a scalar double word. Multi-value
+  results that do not fit those registers use LLVM's hidden result pointer.
+- P2 has hardware locks but no hub-memory atomic read/modify/write instruction.
+  LLVM's atomic expansion pass therefore emits runtime calls. The runtime must
+  implement both sized `__atomic_*_N` and generic byte-range `__atomic_*` entry
+  points. In particular, an i64 object aligned to four bytes can select the
+  generic ABI. Fences call `__sync_synchronize`.
+- Stack-save and stack-restore intrinsics copy the upward-growing PTRA byte
+  pointer. Variable-sized stack allocation remains explicitly unsupported.
+- Promoted boolean conditions have zero upper bits, so branches and selects
+  test the low bit after integer-to-i1 truncation. Boolean memory values use
+  byte loads with the requested extension. Paired
+  unsigned 64-bit division and remainder share one `__udivmoddi4` runtime call.
+- Native REV and ABS instructions implement their 32-bit LLVM operations.
+  Unsigned QMUL implements the low/high product; signed-high multiplication
+  requires the corresponding sign corrections. CLZ must handle zero before
+  relying on ENCOD.
+- Inline assembly in Clang implicitly clobbers the status register `sw`. This
+  prevents a C comparison from being reused across assembly that changes C/Z.
+- STALLI, ALLOWI, SETINT1/2/3, COGATN, and RETI1 are accepted by the assembler.
+  The fixed interrupt instructions reject inappropriate WC/WZ suffixes.
+- `llvm.returnaddress(0)` reads the existing CALLA frame word and removes
+  saved condition flags. Cog entry points and unsupported ancestor depths return
+  null; the backend does not invent a frame chain.
+- `llvm.trap` uses LLVM's `abort` libcall. A freestanding runtime must provide
+  its own non-returning `abort` implementation.
+
+## Validation
+
+Use the source tree corresponding to the actual build, rather than the legacy
+LLVM submodule:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/run.py --build-dir ../llvm15-build --llvm-source llvm15
+```
+
+The instruction matrix checks encodings against the independent Rev B
+instruction table. Code-generation and assembler tests establish compiler
+behavior; physical board fixtures are still required to establish execution
+correctness, multicore ordering, and timing.
